From 6236cf0f2bb2d8a42b6263b677186385265fb257 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vinu Bharath R <vinubhar@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:38:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Airties: Populate Boot ID from device state

Replace the random Airties DeviceInfo boot_id with a value derived from the
platform boot identifier.

Add a BPL cfg_get_device_boot_id() API and implement it for:
- DM backend using the latest Device.DeviceInfo.Reboots timestamp
- UCI backend using /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id
- dummy backend with a false fallback

Use the platform boot ID in both Airties TLV implementations and fall back to
boot_id=1 if the device value cannot be read or converts to zero.

Signed-off-by: Vinu Bharath R <vinubhar@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
